WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.184 --> 00:00:13.247
Tina: What do you mean, “It’s not from this world”?

2
00:00:13.267 --> 00:00:15.407
Brad: It’s not from this world.

3
00:00:16.048 --> 00:00:16.968
I checked the Internet.

4
00:00:16.988 --> 00:00:19.268
Brad: We don’t have clay like that.

5
00:00:19.288 --> 00:00:22.709
Danny: I told you I was telling the truth!

6
00:00:22.729 --> 00:00:29.251
Tina: So this clay was given to you by a giant?

7
00:00:29.271 --> 00:00:32.252
Danny: I told you his name is Hopian.

8
00:00:33.052 --> 00:00:34.572
Brad: And what are you supposed to do?

9
00:00:34.592 --> 00:00:39.254
Danny: We’re supposed to help bring back the lost color to his world!

10
00:00:39.274 --> 00:00:41.874
Tina: And how are we going to do this?

11
00:00:41.894 --> 00:00:44.895
Danny: He told me to remember something.

12
00:00:44.915 --> 00:00:49.857
Danny: He said, “Your imagination can unlock any door.”

13
00:00:49.877 --> 00:00:53.118
Tina: Your imagination?

14
00:00:53.138 --> 00:00:54.878
Danny: Yes.

15
00:00:55.738 --> 00:00:57.519
Brad: Can unlock any door?

16
00:00:57.539 --> 00:00:58.879
Danny: Yes.

17
00:00:58.899 --> 00:01:01.120
Brad: What does that mean?

18
00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:03.041
Danny: I don’t know!

19
00:01:03.061 --> 00:01:06.643
Tina: This is crazy.

20
00:01:06.663 --> 00:01:09.084
Brad: Wait a second.

21
00:01:09.924 --> 00:01:11.905
It’s got to be some sort of riddle.

22
00:01:11.925 --> 00:01:13.186
Tina: And?

23
00:01:13.206 --> 00:01:16.568
Brad: My computer can solve any problem.

24
00:01:16.588 --> 00:01:20.830
Danny: So what does it say?

25
00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:26.533
Brad: Maybe I’m not putting it in right.

26
00:01:26.553 --> 00:01:29.355
Tina: Any answer is better than nothing.

27
00:01:29.915 --> 00:01:30.756
What does it say?

28
00:01:34.648 --> 00:01:36.410
Brad: “Every door is different.”

29
00:01:39.552 --> 00:01:41.233
Tina: Hey, I’ve got an idea.

30
00:01:41.954 --> 00:01:49.800
Tina: Maybe if we look at it long enough, we’ll figure it out.

31
00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:52.683
Brad: I can barely read that.

32
00:01:52.703 --> 00:01:55.124
Tina: You know what it says!

33
00:01:55.144 --> 00:01:57.947
Danny: Hey, don’t fight.

34
00:02:02.751 --> 00:02:03.992
Maybe it’s up to me.

35
00:02:05.036 --> 00:02:07.518
Tina: He did say, “Your imagination.”

36
00:02:07.538 --> 00:02:10.521
Brad: And you have this special clay to help.

37
00:02:10.801 --> 00:02:13.023
Right? Danny: That’s it!

38
00:02:13.384 --> 00:02:14.965
Tina: What’s it?

39
00:02:14.985 --> 00:02:17.648
Danny: Stand back and watch!

40
00:02:18.969 --> 00:02:21.291
Brad: Oh great.

41
00:02:21.871 --> 00:02:22.512
Who are you?

42
00:02:22.932 --> 00:02:23.753
Harry Potter?

43
00:02:23.773 --> 00:02:30.960
Danny: ALA KAZAAM KABLAM, TAKE ME TO GINORMOUS!

44
00:02:35.448 --> 00:02:37.029
Brad: Um didn’t work.

45
00:02:37.430 --> 00:02:39.591
Tina: We’re still in the bushes, Danny.

46
00:02:39.611 --> 00:02:43.635
Danny: My imagination isn’t that great, I guess.

47
00:02:43.975 --> 00:02:49.579
Brad: Only two more minutes of recess left!

48
00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:52.342
Tina: Yeah, we don’t want to be late.

49
00:02:52.682 --> 00:02:53.222
Let’s go!

50
00:02:53.242 --> 00:03:00.308
Danny: What’s that sound?

51
00:03:00.328 --> 00:03:02.430
Tina: It’s just my keys.

52
00:03:02.650 --> 00:03:04.791
Hurry! Danny: WAIT!
